Two lived in supply_chain.py and disagreed, and the MORE DESTRUCTIVE consumer
held the WEAKER rule. is_likely_minified heuristic 3 was an unanchored
case-insensitive (Generated by|@generated|DO NOT EDIT) over five lines, and it
decides Tier.DERIVED, which drops EVERY SYMBOL IN THE FILE; the comment-anchored
_GENERATED_HEADER_PATTERN only set the is_generated flag. _classify_file_core
consults the loose one at step 2 and returns immediately, so the loose one won.

MEASURED COST, both from the items' own filings:
  INV-bokim  two hand-written first-party test files in THIS repository
             contributed ZERO nodes to a default survey, because their
             DOCSTRINGS mention some other file being regenerated --
             "regenerated by" contains "generated by" -- with test_ir.py
             (186 nodes) as the control that showed the survey was working.
  INV-pogob  a Go probe reported 0 of 210 primitives reachable because its own
             fixture carried `// generated by <script>`; only the instrument's
             positive control stopped that number from shipping.

THE UNION IS THE RULE, NOT THE STRICT SET. Collapsing onto
_GENERATED_HEADER_PATTERN as it stood would have LOST a real detection: the
Python protobuf compiler writes "# Generated by the protocol buffer compiler.
DO NOT EDIT!", which is not "Code generated by". The shared rule is
comment-anchored and keeps the weak phrase "generated by" ONLY when DO NOT EDIT
co-occurs on the same line -- what separates a generator's declaration from a
sentence about one.

THE SCOPE IS THE LEADING COMMENT BLOCK, and a first cut got that wrong in a way
only measurement caught. Scanning the whole 4 KiB head for an anchored marker
passed every unit test and newly classified three FIRST-PARTY files as
generated on a five-repo sweep:
    test_max_tier.py:106              # ...via its "DO NOT EDIT" header,
    BaseToggleActionDelegate.java:38  // TODO Auto-generated method stub
    CloverModuleConfig.java:41        // autogenerated
The first is INV-bokim's defect wearing a comment instead of a docstring; the
second is Eclipse's per-METHOD stub marker. A generated file declares itself in
its HEADER, so the header is the scope -- and it must be the BLOCK rather than
the first five lines, because a real declaration routinely sits under a licence
notice (http4s MimeDB.scala, line 17, under 15 lines of Apache). All three are
pinned as regressions, with the licence-header case as the control.

